 "comments": [
  {
   "address": 2304,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "The five events' entry addresses, which load_event jumps to once the event's file is in: 100m Slither $0B00, Space Hockey $0B01, Psychic Judo $1C14, Head Throwing $1000, Metamorph Marathon $1F9F."
  },
  {
   "address": 2305,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Its high bytes interleaved: Slither's."
  },
  {
   "address": 2313,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "event_sides is read from here, as $0909 + the event's number (1 to 5)."
  },
  {
   "address": 2314,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "The disk side each event's file is on, read as $0909 + the event's number: 0 for the first side (Slither, Hockey), 1 for the second (Judo, Head Throwing, Marathon)."
  },
  {
   "address": 2319,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "The file name \"0:PROG0\", its digit set to the event's number less 1."
  },
  {
   "address": 2325,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "The name's digit."
  },
  {
   "address": 2326,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Loads event $04 and runs it: unhooks the menu's interrupt ($1082), takes the entry address from $0900 into the JMP at $0970, puts the digit into the name, switches to the ROM character set, prints \"EVENT LOADING / PLEASE WAIT\", and loads the file from drive 8 through the resident loader at $0800."
  },
  {
   "address": 2409,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "After the load: status $40 (the end of the file reached) runs the event through the JMP; anything else prints the disk message and waits for a key."
  },
  {
   "address": 2416,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "The JMP to the event's entry, its operand set by load_event."
  },
  {
   "address": 2417,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "The JMP's operand, low byte."
  },
  {
   "address": 2418,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "The JMP's operand, high byte."
  },
  {
   "address": 2419,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Prints \"PLEASE ENSURE THAT THE GALACTIC GAMES DISK\" and the side it should be ($09FB label side up, $0A1F label side down, by $08FF), then \"PRESS ANY KEY TO CONTINUE\"; waits for a key to be let go and pressed, clears the screen and loads again."
  },
  {
   "address": 2509,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "The disk message's three parts, each ended by $FF: the first line, \"IS LABEL SIDE UP IN THE DRIVE.\" ($09FB) and \"IS LABEL SIDE DOWN IN THE DRIVE.\" ($0A1F)."
  },
  {
   "address": 2555,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "\"DISK IS LABEL SIDE UP IN THE DRIVE.\", ended by $FF."
  },
  {
   "address": 2591,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "\"DISK IS LABEL SIDE DOWN IN THE DRIVE.\", ended by $FF."
  },
  {
   "address": 2629,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "\"PRESS ANY KEY TO CONTINUE\", ended by $FF."
  },
  {
   "address": 2667,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "The loading screen: clear screen, light blue, \"EVENT LOADING\" and \"PLEASE WAIT\", ended by $FF."
  },
  {
   "address": 2730,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Left over and called by nothing: the end of a serial-bus routine and two banking routines from a build of the loader, up to $0AEF."
  },
  {
   "address": 2800,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Left over: sixteen bytes after it."
  },
  {
   "address": 2816,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "The commentator's ball: fourteen sprite shapes, $2C to $39, 64 bytes each."
  },
  {
   "address": 2880,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Ball shape $2D."
  },
  {
   "address": 2944,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Ball shape $2E."
  },
  {
   "address": 3008,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Ball shape $2F."
  },
  {
   "address": 3042,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Part of ball shape $2F."
  },
  {
   "address": 3072,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Ball shape $30."
  },
  {
   "address": 3136,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Ball shape $31."
  },
  {
   "address": 3200,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Ball shape $32."
  },
  {
   "address": 3264,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Ball shape $33."
  },
  {
   "address": 3328,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Ball shape $34."
  },
  {
   "address": 3392,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Ball shape $35."
  },
  {
   "address": 3456,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Ball shape $36."
  },
  {
   "address": 3520,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Ball shape $37."
  },
  {
   "address": 3584,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Ball shape $38."
  },
  {
   "address": 3648,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Ball shape $39."
  },
  {
   "address": 3712,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "The first entry, after the intro: banks the ROMs out ($2550), clears the championship flag ($B800), the last event ($FF), the disk side ($08FF) and the records-changed flag ($08FE), then goes on as menu_return."
  },
  {
   "address": 3728,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "The entry from an event's quit: sets up three voices that sound only while the volume is up, which is how the typing clicks, the colours and the character set at $2800 ($D018 = $1A), prints message 0, hooks the interrupt ($1064), and has the commentator say the line for the event just played (message $FF + 1: 1 the welcome after the intro, 2 to 6 after each event). FIRE skips to $0F18."
  },
  {
   "address": 3864,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "In the championship ($B800 set), the next event loads by itself, or after the marathon the championship ends; otherwise the records are saved if they changed ($0F41) and the menu runs ($0FF4)."
  },
  {
   "address": 3905,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Saves the records: asks for the first side when the second is in (messages 15, 16 and 20, waiting for FIRE), shows \"SAVING RECORDS TO DISK\", deletes the file RECO (\"S:RECO\" on the command channel), and saves $BC64-$BC95 as RECO; on a disk error says \"ERROR WHILE SAVING RECORDS\" and tries again."
  },
  {
   "address": 4070,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "\"S:RECO\", the command that deletes the records file; its last four bytes ($0FE8) are the file name RECO."
  },
  {
   "address": 4076,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Saved: the ball hooked again and the disk marked as the first side ($08FF = 0)."
  },
  {
   "address": 4084,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Runs the menu ($2385); choice 6 is the championship, which starts with event 1 and $B800 set; any other loads that event."
  },
  {
   "address": 4106,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Starts event $04: FIRE skips to load_event; if the event's file is on the other side, asks for that side (message 15, then 16 or 17); then waits three seconds, has the commentator describe the event (message $04 + 9) and loads it."
  },
  {
   "address": 4182,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "The text cursor's column, which the ball follows."
  },
  {
   "address": 4183,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "The text cursor's row, which the ball follows."
  },
  {
   "address": 4184,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Twelve bytes nothing reads."
  },
  {
   "address": 4196,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Points the KERNAL's interrupt vector at the ball's handler ($1120) and turns on sprites 0 to 4, sprite 4 multicolour and twice the size."
  },
  {
   "address": 4226,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Gives the interrupt vector back ($1243) and turns the sprites off."
  },
  {
   "address": 4256,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Waits for the raster to pass line 256: the bottom of the screen."
  },
  {
   "address": 4267,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Puts the ball's five sprites at the text cursor: pointers from $1116 and colours from $111B; X from the cursor's column, Y from its row, and $14 higher while the click sounds, so the ball hops at each letter."
  },
  {
   "address": 4374,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "The ball's five sprite pointers; the third ($1118) is the spinning frame."
  },
  {
   "address": 4376,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "The third sprite's pointer: the spinning shape."
  },
  {
   "address": 4379,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "The ball's five sprite colours."
  },
  {
   "address": 4384,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "The ball's interrupt, every frame before the KERNAL's own: steps the ball's spin through the list at $11E0; every three frames clicks (volume up) when the cursor has moved a column or a row, and moves the ball to it ($10AB); every two frames steps sprite multicolour 2 through the list at $11D7."
  },
  {
   "address": 4564,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "The click's frame count ($11D4, 3), the colour's frame count ($11D5, 2) and place in its list ($11D6)."
  },
  {
   "address": 4565,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "The colour's frame count."
  },
  {
   "address": 4566,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "The place in the colour list."
  },
  {
   "address": 4567,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "The colours the ball flashes through, ended by $FF."
  },
  {
   "address": 4572,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "A byte nothing reads."
  },
  {
   "address": 4573,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "The cursor's column ($11DD) and row ($11DE) at the last click."
  },
  {
   "address": 4574,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "The row at the last click."
  },
  {
   "address": 4575,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "The place in the spin list."
  },
  {
   "address": 4576,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "The ball's spin: pairs of a sprite shape and the frames it shows, ended by $FF."
  },
  {
   "address": 4673,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "ball_irq's work: the cursor's line address less $0400, counted down by 40 to its row."
  },
  {
   "address": 4674,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Its high byte."
  },
  {
   "address": 4675,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "The KERNAL's interrupt vector, saved by menu_return."
  },
  {
   "address": 4676,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "The saved vector's high byte."
  },
  {
   "address": 4677,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "The frames left of the spin's current shape."
  },
  {
   "address": 4678,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "The commentator says message A: banks the ROMs in, then types the message a character at a time through CHROUT, with a pause after each ($13C3): two frames for a letter, three for a space, twenty for \"$\"; $0C clears the text ($1333) and $0D starts a new line ($12FE). FIRE on any device can skip the rest ($12DB)."
  },
  {
   "address": 4827,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "FIRE while the commentator speaks: ignored while $07 is set (from the end of the comment after an event); otherwise silences the click, prints message 0, and jumps through ($08), throwing away the stack."
  },
  {
   "address": 4862,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "A new line: slides the ball back to column 2, then moves the cursor down a row, scrolling the text up ($1378) when it is on the last row ($13C2)."
  },
  {
   "address": 4915,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Clears the text: rows 1 to 18 blanked and the ball slid back to column 2, row 2."
  },
  {
   "address": 4984,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Scrolls rows 2 to 18 of the screen and of colour RAM up one row."
  },
  {
   "address": 5057,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "A byte between scroll_text and last_row, read by nothing."
  },
  {
   "address": 5058,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "The commentator's last row, 18."
  },
  {
   "address": 5059,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Waits X frames, one fewer when bit 7 of $13D0 is set."
  },
  {
   "address": 5072,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "pause's flag: counted down when the menu runs and up when an event starts."
  },
  {
   "address": 5073,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "The addresses of the commentator's 21 messages, numbered from 0."
  },
  {
   "address": 5074,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "The message addresses' high bytes, interleaved."
  },
  {
   "address": 5115,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Message 0, nothing: clear screen and light blue, used to blank the text, ended by $FF."
  },
  {
   "address": 5121,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Message 1, the welcome: \"WELCOME GALACTI-SPORT FANS TO THE MEGA EVENT OF THE CENTURY......\", ended by $FF."
  },
  {
   "address": 5796,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Message 2, after 100m Slither: \"OKAY, THAT WAS THE 100M SLITHER OR 'SLITH' AS WE PROFESSIONALS CALL...\", ended by $FF."
  },
  {
   "address": 5913,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Message 3, after Space Hockey: \"HEY! THAT PUCK IS NICE CHAP REALLY! YOU DIDN'T HAVE TO BASH THE...\", ended by $FF."
  },
  {
   "address": 6015,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Message 4, after Psychic Judo: \"QUITE A PSYCHIC EXPERIENCE, HUH? WELL, WHEN YOU'VE RECOVERED HOW...\", ended by $FF."
  },
  {
   "address": 6127,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Message 5, after Head Throwing: \"WELL, YOU OBVIOUSLY DIDN'T LOSE YOUR HEAD OVER THAT ONE! NOW TRY...\", ended by $FF."
  },
  {
   "address": 6294,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Message 6, after Metamorph Marathon: \"THAT REALLY WAS A GOOD EFFORT. BUT IT'S VERY DIFFICULT TO CRACK THE...\", ended by $FF."
  },
  {
   "address": 6423,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Message 7, the menu: \"SPACE HOCKEY PSYCHIC JUDO HEAD THROWING METAMORPH MARATHON GALACTIC...\", ended by $FF."
  },
  {
   "address": 6587,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Message 8, empty, ended by $FF."
  },
  {
   "address": 6593,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Message 9, empty, ended by $FF."
  },
  {
   "address": 6595,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Message 10, 100m Slither described: \"HOLD TIGHT AS WE DESCEND INTO THE MAIN STADIUM FOR THE 100M SLITHER....\", ended by $FF."
  },
  {
   "address": 7244,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Message 11, Space Hockey described: \"NOT AN OPTICAL ILLUSION! HERE IS YOUR CHANCE TO BE AN EYE WITNESS TO...\", ended by $FF."
  },
  {
   "address": 7600,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Message 12, Psychic Judo described: \"MIND GAMES FOR THOSE WITH A STRONG STOMACH! KNOWN AS THE BELCHING...\", ended by $FF."
  },
  {
   "address": 8017,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Message 13, Head Throwing described: \"THOSE HUNKY HURLING HRUNTANS FROM THE PLANET JAVELOS ARE STICKING...\", ended by $FF."
  },
  {
   "address": 8224,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Message 13 goes on."
  },
  {
   "address": 8318,
